### 1.2 Network Connectivity

The required network paths must be available before starting the OKD installation.

Required connectivity includes:

```text
Bastion
   │
   ├──→ Bootstrap
   ├──→ Masters
   └──→ Workers

OCI Load Balancer
   │
   ├──→ Bootstrap / Masters
   └──→ Workers

Private Nodes
   │
   └──→ Internet through NAT Gateway
```

#### Verify Bastion → Private Nodes

From the Bastion:

```bash
ping -c 3 <bootstrap-ip>
ping -c 3 <master-ip>
ping -c 3 <worker-ip>
```

Then verify SSH:

```bash
ssh <user>@<bootstrap-ip>
ssh <user>@<master-ip>
ssh <user>@<worker-ip>
```

> ICMP/ping may be blocked by security rules. A failed ping does not automatically mean TCP connectivity is unavailable. SSH or `nc` provides a more useful test for the required ports.

#### Verify required ports

From the Bastion:

```bash
nc -vz <master-ip> 6443
nc -vz <master-ip> 22623
nc -vz <worker-ip> 80
nc -vz <worker-ip> 443
```

#### Verify private-node outbound connectivity

From a private node:

```bash
curl -I https://www.google.com
```

If DNS is also being tested:

```bash
curl -I https://quay.io
```

#### Expected result

For reachable TCP ports:

```text
Connection to <IP> <port> port [tcp/*] succeeded!
```

For outbound HTTPS:

```text
HTTP/...
```

or another valid HTTP response.

