### 1.3 DNS

OKD requires working DNS for API, internal API, and application routes.

The lab uses:

```text
ocp.lab
```

Important names include:

```text
api.okd.ocp.lab
api-int.okd.ocp.lab
*.apps.okd.ocp.lab
```

#### Verify DNS resolution

From the Bastion:

```bash
dig api.okd.ocp.lab
dig api-int.okd.ocp.lab
dig console-openshift-console.apps.okd.ocp.lab
dig oauth-openshift.apps.okd.ocp.lab
```

For the wildcard application domain:

```bash
dig console-openshift-console.apps.okd.ocp.lab
dig oauth-openshift.apps.okd.ocp.lab
```

Both should resolve to the OCI Load Balancer IP.

For example:

```text
console-openshift-console.apps.okd.ocp.lab
        │
        ▼
OCI Private DNS
        │
        ▼
130.210.21.43
```

You can also query a specific DNS server:

```bash
dig @<DNS-SERVER-IP> api.okd.ocp.lab
```

#### Verify reverse DNS if configured

```bash
dig -x <load-balancer-ip>
```

Reverse DNS is not required for the basic OKD installation unless you have specifically configured it.

